.nh
.TH "AUTOSNAP" "1" "Jun 2026" "autosnap" "autosnap manual"

.SH NAME
autosnap-list - List checkpoints


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBautosnap list [checkpoint-or-range] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List checkpoints.

.PP
A range A..B lists checkpoints from A through B, inclusive. Ranges are
inclusive autosnap checkpoint intervals, not general Git revision ranges.

.PP
The checkpoint argument can be an explicit autosnap ref, a checkpoint commit hash,
or one of these current-branch history selectors:

.PP
first
  first+N
  last
  last-N


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	List checkpoints for all branches

.PP
\fB--branch\fP=""
	List checkpoints for a specific branch

.PP
\fB--format\fP="text"
	Output format: text, json, jsonl

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--note-ref\fP=""
	Git notes ref for checkpoint notes

.PP
\fB--notes\fP[=false]
	Include checkpoint git notes as text

.PP
\fB--notes-json\fP[=false]
	Include checkpoint git notes decoded as JSON (requires --format json or jsonl)

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	List checkpoints since a duration or commit ID


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBautosnap(1)\fP
